<article class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="reveal">
<p>Xinjiang is China's largest and most diverse region — a land of snow-capped mountains, vast deserts, emerald grasslands, and ancient oasis cities. Stretching over 1.6 million square kilometers (one-sixth of China's total area), Xinjiang offers travelers an unparalleled mix of natural wonders and cultural richness. This complete guide covers everything you need to plan your Xinjiang adventure in 2026.</p>

<div style="background:var(--cream);padding:24px;border-radius:12px;margin:32px 0;">
